# Normalize line endings on checkin, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# Not cosmetic. A Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every file to CRLF, and tooling
# that reads sources line by line then sees a trailing \r on every line. The seam-documentation
# check in scripts/validate-manifests.mjs was written against \n and would have failed all seven
# packages with a message blaming their documentation — a gate reporting a real defect for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the code.
#
# The check itself now tolerates CRLF (it splits on /\r?\n/), which is the right fix for a tool
# reading arbitrary input. This file is the other half: the repository states what it stores, so
# every other tool that has not been hardened does not have to be.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated. Marked so a lockfile conflict does not arrive as a 10,000-line review.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
